<% provide(:title, "Privacy & Security") %>

<div class="container py-5">
  <div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9">
      <h1 class="h2 mb-3">Privacy &amp; Security Architecture</h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted mb-4">
        ShareMyBag Exchange is engineered to OWASP ASVS and enterprise aviation security standards, protecting passenger PNR privacy and order book integrity.
      </p>

      <div class="d-grid gap-4">
        <section class="smb-card p-4">
          <h2 class="h5 mb-2">PNR Isolation &amp; Anti-IDOR Controls</h2>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
            Passenger PNR references, email addresses, and voucher wallet balances are strictly scoped to the authenticated account holder. Public profiles and flight order books never expose counterparty emails or PNR codes. Every order creation and cancellation verifies ownership server-side.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="smb-card p-4">
          <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Order Book Integrity &amp; Concurrency Safety</h2>
          <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
            Every trade executes inside an atomic PostgreSQL transaction with deterministic pessimistic locking (Flight → PassengerBooking → resting KiloOrders). Built-in safeguards prevent double-selling (overdrafting PNR kg), wash trading (self-matching or holding opposite orders on the same flight), and exceeding aircraft payload limits.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="smb-card p-4">
          <h2 class="h5 mb-2">Hardened Web &amp; Session Security (OWASP)</h2>
          <ul class="text-muted small mb-0 d-grid gap-1">
            <li>Strong password policy with BCrypt hashing and session fixation prevention (<code>reset_session</code> on sign-in).</li>
            <li><code>HttpOnly</code>, <code>SameSite=Lax</code>, and <code>Secure</code> cookies with SHA-256 rotated remember tokens.</li>
            <li>Strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> (zero inline scripts or inline styles), <code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code>, <code>X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff</code>, and restrictive <code>Permissions-Policy</code>.</li>
            <li><code>Rack::Attack</code> rate limiting on authentication, registration, and order book submission endpoints.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
